# 36 posix  SOCK_STREAM accept()ed socket custom setsockopt() — disabled: environmental, not a guest bug. In forward the server is the HOST Linux kernel (6.12 without the fix), whose setsockopt(SO_ZEROCOPY) on the accept()ed socket fails EOPNOTSUPP — the very kernel bug this upstream test was written for; the Windows client side passes ("36 ... ok"). Our bodies run in reverse + loopback. Re-enable on hosts with the fixed kernel.
